---
// Privacy policy (WWW-5, DP-1 to DP-3). Drafted by the dev team; the client reviews it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT, LEGAL_VERSION, readSettings } from '../settings.ts';

const s = readSettings(process.env);
const updated = new Date(`${LEGAL_VERSION}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How OmniBridge processes personal data: who we are, what we process and why, retention, sub-processors, transfers, security and your rights."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated} (version {LEGAL_VERSION})</p>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      OmniBridge is a back-office service for UK sellers, operated by {s.operatorLegalName}, company
      number {s.operatorCompanyNumber}, registered office {s.operatorRegisteredAddress} (“we”, “us”).
    </p>
    <p>
      Each business that uses OmniBridge (a “workspace customer”) is the <strong>controller</strong>
      of its own customers’ and staff data. We process that data on its behalf as its
      <strong>processor</strong>, under the data processing terms that form part of our
      <a href="/terms">terms of service</a>. For eBay data, eBay’s terms treat us as an independent
      controller. For our own account and billing contacts, we are the controller.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What data we process and where it comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>From Amazon and Amazon Ads:</strong> orders, buyer names, delivery addresses and
        phone numbers, buyer messages received through Amazon’s buyer–seller email relay, seller
        feedback, account health, advertising and fee data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>From eBay:</strong> orders, buyer names and delivery addresses, messages and
        feedback.
      </li>
      <li><strong>From the workspace customer’s own website:</strong> orders and delivery details.</li>
      <li><strong>From carriers (Evri, DPD):</strong> labels, tracking and delivery events.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>From users of OmniBridge:</strong> name, work email, sign-in records (time and IP
        address), and what they do in the service (the audit log).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Why we process it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        To provide the service the workspace customer asked for: dispatching and tracking orders,
        managing stock, answering buyers, reporting profit and VAT figures (contract and the
        customer’s instructions).
      </li>
      <li>To keep the service and its users secure, including sign-in and audit records (legitimate interests).</li>
      <li>To keep finance records the law requires (legal obligation).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell data, use it for advertising or profile buyers.</p>

    <h2>4. The 30-day rule for buyers’ details</h2>
    <p>
      Buyers’ personal details are deleted within 30 days of delivery, from every copy including
      backups. The live copy goes 25 days after delivery. Orders that are cancelled lose their
      personal details once the cancellation is confirmed. Buyer messages are deleted 30 days after
      the conversation’s last activity.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long we keep data</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Buyers’ personal details on delivered orders</td><td>Gone from every copy by 30 days after delivery</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Buyer messages</td><td>30 days after the conversation’s last activity</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Order records without personal details, VAT and finance records</td><td>6 years after the end of the VAT period</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Expenses and invoices</td><td>6 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Amazon data after a seller disconnects or revokes access</td><td>Deleted within 30 days (finance records without personal details are kept as the law requires)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>eBay data after an account deletion notice</td><td>Deleted within 30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Audit and security logs</td><td>6 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Notifications</td><td>12 months</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>6. Who else processes data for us (sub-processors)</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Who</th><th>What for</th><th>Where</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>netcup GmbH</td><td>Server hosting</td><td>Germany</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Scaleway SAS (Transactional Email)</td><td>Sending system email (invitations, password resets, alerts)</td><td>EU (France)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Zoho Corporation (Zoho Mail)</td><td>Our mailboxes, including the inbound addresses for Amazon’s buyer–seller email relay</td><td>EU data centre</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Evri and DPD</td><td>Delivering parcels; they receive delivery details as carriers</td><td>United Kingdom</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Our development team</td><td>Building and supporting the service, under an International Data Transfer Agreement</td><td>Pakistan</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Data is hosted in the EU. Our development team works from Pakistan, which has no UK adequacy
      decision; access from there is covered by the ICO’s International Data Transfer Agreement and
      limited to what support needs. Buyers’ personal details are kept in a separate encrypted store.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Data travels over HTTPS. Buyers’ personal details are encrypted with a key for each workspace.
      Every user signs in with two-step verification, access is limited to the tabs and companies
      each user is given, and every access to full buyer details is logged. More on our
      <a href="/security">security page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, to object to or restrict
      its processing, and to data portability. If you are a buyer, the seller you bought from is the
      controller: you can ask them, or email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.privacy}`}
        >{CONTACT.privacy}</a
      > and we will pass your request on and help them answer it within one month.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact and complaints</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.privacy}`}>{CONTACT.privacy}</a> or write to us at {
        s.operatorRegisteredAddress
      }. If you are not happy with our answer you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s
      Office: <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>, or 0303
      123 1113.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When we change this policy we update the date above. Users of OmniBridge are asked to accept a
      materially changed policy at their next sign-in.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
